 ("Ridge regression","Least squares with a penalty on large coefficients. Shrinks everything, drops nothing.","The fix for multicollinearity, and the closed form that makes it Cholesky-friendly."),
 ("Lasso","Least squares with an L1 penalty, which drives some coefficients exactly to zero.","When you want feature selection as part of fitting, not as a separate step."),
 ("Elastic net","Ridge and lasso mixed, so correlated features get selected as a group.","Lasso picks one of a correlated pair arbitrarily; elastic net keeps both."),
 ("Gradient clipping","Capping the gradient's size before the optimiser step.","Exploding gradients in RNNs and transformers. A loss that suddenly goes NaN is the symptom."),
 ("Early stopping","Halting training when validation loss stops improving.","Free regularisation. The follow-up: which checkpoint do you keep, and which split chose it?"),
 ("Learning curve","Error plotted against training-set size, for train and validation.","How you tell underfitting from overfitting, and whether more data would help at all."),
 ("GroupKFold","Cross-validation that keeps all rows from one entity in the same fold.","Any data with repeat users or patients — plain KFold leaks and flatters the score."),
 ("Nested CV","An inner loop for tuning, an outer loop for the honest score.","Why tuning and evaluating on the same folds gives an optimistic number."),
 ("Target encoding","Replacing a category with the mean outcome for that category.","High-cardinality categoricals. Leaks badly unless fitted inside the fold."),
 ("Temperature scaling","Dividing logits by one learned constant to fix overconfidence.","The simplest calibration method — one parameter, fitted on validation, accuracy unchanged."),
 ("Platt scaling","Fitting a logistic regression on top of model scores to turn them into probabilities.","Calibrating an SVM or any model whose scores are not probabilities."),
 ("Reliability diagram","Predicted probability on one axis, observed frequency on the other.","How you show a model is overconfident, rather than just asserting it."),
 ("Expected calibration error","The average gap between predicted confidence and actual accuracy across bins.","The single number for calibration. Bin count changes the answer, which is its weakness."),
 ("Brier score","Mean squared error on probabilities — rewards being both correct and calibrated.","When accuracy hides a model that is right but wildly overconfident."),
 ("MCC","Matthews correlation coefficient — a balanced score that stays honest on skewed classes.","99% negatives. Accuracy says 99%, MCC says near zero."),
 ("Cross-entropy","The loss that penalises confident wrong answers far more than hesitant ones.","The default classification loss, and what perplexity exponentiates."),
 ("Perplexity","How many options the model was effectively choosing between at each token.","Language-model quality in one number. Lower is better; it is exp(cross-entropy)."),
